  "description": "Phasor Vector Symbolic Architecture (VSA) codec: encode numbers and symbols as phasor faces, then bind (per-component complex multiply), unbind, bundle (superpose), and read values back by correlation. Bind on the linear band adds values and on the log band multiplies them, so arithmetic is composition rather than a calculator. Two profiles: a fixed frozen-identity codec for models and a width-configurable SIMD codec for storage and similarity search. CycleHologram adds exact multiset storage over a prime field: a fixed array of power sums that adds, subtracts, and decodes every stored symbol and count exactly up to its capacity (Reed-Solomon syndrome decoding). The shared substrate under Evaluated Applications' holographic database and phasor model library.",
